      "math_academy_id": "e-10042",
      "problem": "The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\geq x) = p,$ where $X$ has a student's $t$-distribution $T_k$ with $k$ degrees of freedom. Given that the random variable $X \\sim T_{9},$ find the value of $x$ such that $P(X \\geq x) = 0.005.$\n\n| $k \\setminus p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $8$ | $1.397$ | $1.860$ | $2.306$ | $2.896$ | $3.355$ |\n| $9$ | $1.383$ | $1.833$ | $2.262$ | $2.821$ | $3.250$ |\n| $10$ | $1.372$ | $1.812$ | $2.228$ | $2.764$ | $3.169$ |",
      "worked_solution": "Since $X \\sim T_{9},$ we focus on the row of the table that corresponds to $k=9.$\n\n| $k \\setminus p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0.005}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $8$ | $1.397$ | $1.860$ | $2.306$ | $2.896$ | $3.355$ |\n| $9$ | $1.383$ | $1.833$ | $2.262$ | $2.821$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{red}3.250}$ |\n| $10$ | $1.372$ | $1.812$ | $2.228$ | $2.764$ | $3.169$ |\n\nFrom this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X \\geq {\\color{red}3.250}) = {\\color{blue}0.005}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=3.250.$",
